\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Third-party notices}\par
\pard\sa120 Arx itself is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (LICENSE). Arx includes the third-party material below. Each licence also travels with the material itself, and the texts this file refers to are in Distribution/Licenses. The app shows this file under About Arx \u8594? Credits ({\f1\fs20 make credits} regenerates {\f1\fs20 Containers/macOS/Credits.rtf} from it).\par
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs24 Browser engine}\par
\pard\sa120 Arx's engine is the Helium browser for macOS, built from source with Arx's own patches ({\f1\fs20 Scripts/engine/}) into {\f1\fs20 Arx Framework.framework}. The pinned versions are in {\f1\fs20 Packages/engine/engine.lock.json}: helium-macos {\f1\fs20 da5fcc2}, Helium {\f1\fs20 a2d96a7}, Chromium 157.0.8103.78.\par
\pard\li240\fi-240\sa60 \bullet\tab {\b Helium} ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/imputnet/helium"}}{\fldrslt https://github.com/imputnet/helium}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/imputnet/helium-macos"}}{\fldrslt https://github.com/imputnet/helium-macos}}) by imput. Helium's own code and patches are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3. Helium's {\f1\fs20 LICENSE} and {\f1\fs20 LICENSE.ungoogled_chromium} files from both pinned repositories are kept unchanged in Packages/engine/Licenses.\par
\pard\li240\fi-240\sa60 \bullet\tab {\b ungoogled-chromium} ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium"}}{\fldrslt https://github.com/ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium}}). Code Helium takes unchanged from ungoogled-chromium stays under the BSD 3-Clause License: Distribution/Licenses/ungoogled-chromium.txt.\par
\pard\li240\fi-240\sa60 \bullet\tab {\b Chromium} ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chromium.org"}}{\fldrslt https://www.chromium.org}}), Copyright The Chromium Authors, under the BSD 3-Clause License: Distribution/Licenses/chromium.txt. {\f1\fs20 Packages/engine/Sources/ChromiumBootstrap/Upstream/} carries Chromium source with the same licence.\par
\pard\li240\fi-240\sa60 \bullet\tab {\b Chromium's third-party components.} Chromium bundles several hundred libraries under their own licences (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0, LGPL, MPL and others). The engine build compiles their full list, with every licence text, into Chromium's {\f1\fs20 chrome://credits} page.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs24 Swift packages}\par
\pard\sa120 These packages are compiled into Arx or its {\f1\fs20 ArxMCP} helper, except swift-snapshot-testing (tests), swift-syntax and swift-macro-toolkit (macros, used while compiling) and package-resources-cli (code generation), which aren't shipped. Versions come from the {\f1\fs20 Package.resolved} files; "fork" means a Git submodule under {\f1\fs20 Forks/}.\par
\pard\sa120 MIT-licensed packages are under the MIT License (Distribution/Licenses/MIT.txt) with the copyright line shown. Apache-2.0 packages are under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (Distribution/Licenses/Apache-2.0.txt). swift-nio and swift-log ship NOTICE files, reproduced in Distribution/Licenses/swift-nio-NOTICE.txt and Distribution/Licenses/swift-log-NOTICE.txt. Sparkle ships as a prebuilt framework inside the app; its licence, with the licences of the bsdiff, sais-lite, Ed25519 and signature-verification code it includes, is reproduced in Distribution/Licenses/Sparkle.txt. The MCP Swift SDK is moving from MIT to Apache-2.0: contributions relicensed so far are under Apache-2.0, the rest stay under the MIT License with the copyright line shown, and both apply to the pinned version.\par
